Q: How can I find out if the event is being catched in the parent component A: <p>In Vue 3 with a component using <code>&lt;script setup&gt;</code>, I had success with the following code:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>import { getCurrentInstance } from &quot;vue&quot;;

const emit = defineEmits&lt;{
    &quot;on-click&quot;: [value: string]
}&gt;();

const instance = getCurrentInstance();

function onClick(value) {
    if (instance?.vnode.props?.onOnClick) {
        emit('on-click', value);
    } else {
        defaultAction();
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>The event name is converted by Vue to camel case and prepended with <code>on</code>. I used the event name <code>on-click</code> from your example, from which Vue makes a prop <code>onOnClick</code>, but of course such an event would normally be called <code>click</code>, from which Vue would make a prop <code>onClick</code>.</p>
